  "title": "Comer Es Bueno --- The Infinitive as Subject",
  "drivablePrefix": 1,
  "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:1ab652191f2cc175",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "ES-C67-comer-es-bueno",
      "sequence": 2555,
      "title": "comer es bueno — the infinitive as the subject",
      "headword": "comer es bueno",
      "romanization": "comer es bueno",
      "gloss": "eating is good — the infinitive standing where a noun would, which is the one job English needs a different form for",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:3174604d9600cf75",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "El libro es grande. A noun, then es, then what it is."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Now put an action in the noun's place."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: the infinitive stands there",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Comer es bueno. — Eating is good. Hablar español es bueno. — Speaking Spanish is good."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The infinitive — the plain dictionary form — simply occupies the subject slot, and the sentence carries on as normal. Nothing is added and nothing changes shape."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Note the verb after it: es, singular. An action counts as one thing, however many words are wrapped around it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "culture-pragmatics",
          "title": "Why it's said this way",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Here is the trap, and it is entirely an English one."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "English uses -ing for this — eating is good — and you have an -ing form now. So it is tempting to reach for comiendo."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Comiendo es bueno. — wrong."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The gerund never does this job in Spanish. It is for an action underway, leaning on estar; it is not a name for the activity. The infinitive is the name."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So the two languages divide the work differently, and Spanish's division is the simpler one: English argues about to eat against eating, and Spanish uses one form for both."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
